gamescope: forward a game's display-mode pick to the parent compositor (quasar #447)

Why. Nested gamescope sizes its output from -W/-H/-r and never asks the parent
for anything: a game that switches resolution is scaled inside gamescope and
the monitor never moves (upstream WaylandBackend.cpp: the connector's GetModes()
is empty, wl_output modes are only read for a VRR refresh guess). The Quasar
compositor advertises the monitor's real modes, each with its own refresh, and
takes a pick through wlr-output-management-unstable-v1; its node agent then
moves the physical display and configures our toplevel at the new size. This
patch is gamescope's half of that contract.

What it does (all inert when the parent has no zwlr_output_manager_v1, or when
GAMESCOPE_QUASAR_MODE_FORWARD=0 -- the manager is then never bound and gamescope
behaves exactly as upstream):

 A. Lists the parent's modes in each of gamescope's Xwaylands' RandR as user
    modes (XRRCreateMode + XRRAddOutputMode, each with a synthetic timing whose
    vertical refresh is the parent's exact mHz), so a game's resolution menu
    shows the monitor's sizes and rates. Modes larger than the Xwayland root are
    left out (RRSetCrtcConfig rejects them).
 B. Watches the focused window for the mode its client applied:
    _QUASAR_XWAYLAND_EMU_MODE (w, h, mHz; set by the companion
    xwayland-quasar-emu-mode.patch), else _XWAYLAND_RANDR_EMU_MONITOR_RECTS
    (stock Xwayland: size only), else a game Xwayland's root that Steam resized
    with GAMESCOPE_XWAYLAND_MODE_CONTROL. After it has held for 300 ms it asks
    the parent for the matching mode (create_configuration on the last done
    serial, enable_head, set_mode, apply). With no pick in front (the game
    exited, Steam has focus) it asks for the session's own mode again. One
    configuration in flight at a time; a mode already sent is not re-sent until
    the parent's current mode changes (covers the echo while the display moves,
    `failed`, and a `succeeded` the agent then declined).
 C. Follows the parent: the toplevel configure that follows a move already sets
    g_nOutputWidth/Height (LibDecor_Frame_Configure, upstream). The patch adds
    the refresh: on a new current mode it sets g_nNestedRefresh and
    g_nOutputRefresh to it, because `-r` pinned g_nNestedRefresh at launch and
    the vblank timer prefers it. Also only the CURRENT wl_output mode now sets
    the output's refresh (the parent lists every mode on wl_output).

The client header comes from the wlroots submodule's
protocol/wlr-output-management-unstable-v1.xml, copied into protocol/ by the
Dockerfile before meson setup (meson's subproject sandbox forbids reading it in
place). Needs libXrandr-devel at build time.

